-- title:
--   Ramification in the Igusa cover: Kummer dichotomy at a place
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a level $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$, and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$. Let $w$ be an integral weight-one form of level $M$ over $k$: a modular form of weight $1$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with a power series over $\mathbb{Z}$ that is its $q$-expansion and whose reduction $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,k$ is nonzero in $k((q))$; write $a = w.\mathrm{hasseRootFn}$ for the inverse of that reduction. Let $K_0 = \mathrm{x1FunctionFieldC}\,k\,M \subseteq k((q))$ be the subfield generated over $k$ by the $q$-expansion ratios for $\Gamma_1(M)$, and let $F = \mathrm{igusaFunctionField}\,K_0\,a$ be the subfield generated over $k$ by $K_0 \cup \{a\}$, with $\iota = \mathrm{incl}$ the inclusion $K_0 \to F$, assumed integral as a ring homomorphism. Let $b \in K_0$ be an element whose image in $k((q))$ is $a^{p-1}$, and let $P$ be a place of $F$ over $k$ (a proper valuation subring of $F$ containing $k$ which is a principal ideal ring). Write $v = P|_{K_0}$ for the place obtained by pulling $P$ back along $\iota$, and $e(P)$ for the ramification index of $P$ along $\iota$, namely the least $n > 0$ of the form $\mathrm{ord}_P(\iota f)$ with $0 \neq f \in K_0$. The assertion is the conjunction of two implications: if $p-1$ divides $\mathrm{ord}_v(b)$ in $\mathbb{Z}$, then $e(P) = 1$; and if $\mathrm{ord}_v(b)$ and $p-1$ are coprime in $\mathbb{Z}$, then $e(P) = p-1$.
--
--   This is the local ramification dichotomy for the Igusa covering $\mathrm{Ig}(M;p) \to X_1(M)$ in characteristic $p$, presented as a Kummer extension of exponent $p-1$ generated by a $(p-1)$-st root of an element of the base field: unramified where the order of that element is divisible by $p-1$, totally ramified where it is prime to $p-1$. It is used to show that the cover is unramified away from the supersingular locus, in [`ModularCurve.ramificationIndex_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_eq_one_of_not_evalAt_mem_ssJSet`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ramificationIndex_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_eq_one_of_not_evalAt_mem_ssJSet).
-- source:
